## Recent Results (indicative)
- GM (head-finetune, 10 tasks): R-IB≈0.998, D-IB≈0.998 (capacity; not retention-safe).
- Even (head-finetune, 10 tasks): R-IB≈0.973, D-IB≈0.961; next-token degraded.
- Even (probe head, 1 task): R-IB≈0.981, D-IB≈0.963; next-token retained (pre≈post).
- Even (probe head, custom tasks, 5 tasks):
  - even_state->1: R-IB≈0.980, D-IB≈0.963
  - even_state->0: R-IB≈0.987, D-IB≈0.963
  - p1_gt_0.5: R-IB≈0.921, D-IB≈0.931
  - length_even (non-causal): R-IB≈1.000, D-IB≈0.000
  - last3_sum_odd: R-IB≈0.730, D-IB≈0.794
  - All with nt_pre≈nt_post (retained) using probe head.

### Head fine-tuning (custom tasks) observations
- Setup: `--tune_scope head` (no probe head), tasks: even_state->1, even_state->0, p1_gt_0.5, length_even, last3_sum_odd.
- Aggregate: R-IB≈0.75 (±0.19), D-IB≈0.74 (±0.19), showing wide variance across tasks.
- Per-task highlights:
  - even_state->1: R-IB≈0.979, D-IB≈0.964; next-token accuracy dropped to ~0.35; argmax0|O≈0.97 (severe shift).
  - even_state->0: R-IB≈0.985, D-IB≈0.958; next-token retained (~0.65 acc).
  - p1_gt_0.5: R-IB≈0.60, D-IB≈0.61; next-token retained.
  - length_even: R-IB≈0.54, D-IB≈0.50; next-token slightly degraded (~0.60 acc).
  - last3_sum_odd: R-IB≈0.64, D-IB≈0.68; next-token slightly degraded (~0.62 acc).
- Takeaway: head-finetune can significantly degrade next-token behavior for some tasks (especially parity mapping that conflicts with LM head), so prefer probe head or retention-aware fine-tuning.

## Metrics
- R-IB: fraction of same-state pairs with identical predictions (higher is better).
- D-IB: 1 − fraction of different-state pairs with identical predictions (higher is better).
- Next-token retention: with `--use_probe_head`, accuracy pre/post should match.

## Next Steps
- If fine-tuning instead of probe head: freeze `energy_head`, tune only last encoder layer (or LoRA), add retention loss (λ·NT CE or KL to base logits), early stop with nt_post threshold.
- Add `--retain_next_token`, `--retain_lambda`, `--freeze_energy_head`, `--tune_encoder_layers` if moving to retention-aware fine-tuning.
